    <system:String x:Key="Str.Stages.LibreTranslateGuideTitle">LibreTranslate Setup Guide</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str.Stages.LibreTranslateGuide" xml:space="preserve">LibreTranslate Setup Guide&#13;&#13;To use LibreTranslate locally, you only need to install it. Translumo will automatically run the server for you.&#13;&#13;Step 1: Prerequisites&#13;Make sure Python is installed on your computer (download from python.org).&#13;&#13;Step 2: Install LibreTranslate&#13;Open your Command Prompt (CMD) or Terminal. Copy and paste the command below, then press Enter:&#13;&#13;> pip install libretranslate&#13;&#13;Step 3: Download Language Models&#13;Make sure the language you selected is downloaded to your local repository. To download a language (e.g., English to Korean), run:&#13;&#13;> argospm update&#13;> argospm install translate-en_ko&#13;> argospm install translate-ko_en&#13;&#13;For a full list of language codes, please visit:&#13;https://docs.libretranslate.com/guides/supported_languages/&#13;&#13;You don't need to manually run the server anymore. Translumo handles it based on your selected languages!</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str.Stages.OnnxGuideTitle">Information</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str.Stages.OnnxGuideText" xml:space="preserve">The app will automatically download the ONNX model for the selected translation direction. This may take a few minutes. If, even after a long time, the Models\YourLanguage folder is still empty, it means the model was not found or could not be downloaded. You can try downloading it manually from the HuggingFace website.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str.Stages.OnnxManualGuide" xml:space="preserve">HOW TO MANUALLY ADD A NEW LANGUAGE MODEL&#13;(e.g., Japanese to Indonesian / ja-id)&#13;&#13;1. Create a folder named 'ja-id' inside the application's 'Models' directory.&#13;&#13;2. Download (from HuggingFace):&#13; - encoder_model.onnx&#13; - decoder_model.onnx&#13; - 'generation_config.json&#13; - 'tokenizer.json' and place them inside the folder.&#13;&#13;3. Open 'tokenizer.json' with Notepad, find the line containing:&#13;   'normalizer': null, and delete it.&#13;&#13;4. Select the corresponding Source and Target languages in the app above to use it!</system:String>

